= Who will lead the <span style="color: [+ nsdap_colour +];">**NSDAP**</span> now?

[? if hitler_deported: The deported *Führer* has tried to steer the party from Austrian exile before disappearing unexpectedly. Furthermore the left-wing of the party around Joseph Goebbelshas even called for officially condemming the "little bourgeois" whos politcal line was too impure for a true national worker's party. ?]

[? if hitler_dead: The death of Hitler is widely mourned with several factions claiming to represent his legacy. ?]

- @strasser_duh: Gregor Strasser will lead the party.

@strasser_duh
face-image:img/portraits/strasser.jpg
on-arrival: nsdap_leader = "Strasser"; nsdap_ideology = "National Socialism"

With Hermann Göring being abroad and most other participants of the coup imprisonned, the natural leader of the <span style="color: [+ nsdap_colour +];">**NSDAP**</span> appears to be Gregor Strasser, a pharmacist who is both set on maintaining the National Socialist party line of the base and to opening the party towards cooperation with other parties of the <span style="color: [+ nsdap_colour +];">*Völkisch*</span> movement - be they more bourgeois.

Anti-bourgeois purists like Hermann Esser are outraged about the loss of purity but no one listens anyway, so we don't care either...













































